  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Charities Housing filed two 2026 competitive 9% tax credit applications, CA-26-034 and CA-26-066. Neither appears in CTCAC's first-round (June 22, 2026) or second-round (Oct. 6, 2026) preliminary recommendations; the South and West Bay region had no first-round recommendation and Winchester Blvd Apartments in the second.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003608",
        "SRC-003602",
        "SRC-003599",
        "SRC-003609",
        "SRC-003610"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the DDA, closing waits on full financing; if tax credits are not won in the first 2026 round the developer may apply again, and either party may end the DDA after two failed attempts. The staff report projected closing around January 2027 and about 24 months of construction.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003600"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Plaintiffs allege rushed approvals, skipped environmental review and improper use of public land; a Superior Court judge denied a request to halt the project at the end of March 2026. The project removes 89 public parking spaces.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003603"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Site is an 860 by 38 foot strip of the Mary Avenue right-of-way next to Highway 85; buildings are 23 feet tall.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003600"
      ]
    }
  ],
